  "body": "**Stacked on #640** (#630, tool orientation and the shared CL → control-point conversion). Review only this PR's own commit, `22658499`.\n\n**P1 (#641):** grooving and parting posted the **middle of the blade's tip edge**, but a blade is touched off on a **corner**. With a left-corner touch-off, a groove landed w/2 off in Z and a part-off left the part w/2 short.\n- **Verified on the kernels:** `blade.rs` plunges at band centres; `parting.rs` plunges at the parting plane, with the kerf at ±w/2.\n- **Verified on the old golden:** a 3.2 groove from Z-3.6 to Z-6.8 cut with a 2 mm blade posted Z-4.6 and Z-5.8.\n\n## What changed\n- **Blades reuse #630's `orientation`,** read on the LinuxCNC chart. There is no new field or file key, and the same editor row and undoable `ChangeTool` apply.\n  - **1**: the right corner (+Z).\n  - **2**: the left corner (−Z). This is the **default**, from LinuxCNC Lathe User Information §4.2's parting example, a blade touched off on its left side.\n  - **6**: the width centre, the old behaviour. **9** is read as 6.\n- **Conversion:** `posting_nose.rs` shifts GrooveRough, GrooveFinish and Part paths by (0, ±w/2) through #640's rigid `control_point_path`.\n  - X does not move: the CL radius is already the tip line.\n  - There is no corner-radius term: a rounded corner's imaginary tip is the sharp corner.\n- **Refused by name:** codes 3, 4, 5, 7 and 8 (ID or face), and a blade with no usable width.\n- **Unchanged:** the cache, verifier, stock sim and gouge laws keep the true blade. The parting plane still means the kerf centre.\n- **Editor:** a Groove tool's row reads \"Touched-off corner\" and offers only 1, 2 and 6. The tool note prints `ORIENTATION q`.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/641-blade-corner.md`.\n\n**Behaviour change for existing programs:** the left-corner default moves every grooving and parting program by −w/2 in Z. A shop that touched off on the width centre sets its blades to 6.\n\n## Golden diff (`fanuc-lathe/groove_part.nc`)\n- **2 mm groove:** Z-5.8/-4.6 → **Z-6.8/-5.6**, the left corners at the walls.\n- **3 mm part-off:** Z-10 → **Z-11.5**.\n- Clearances move by the same amount; X is unchanged.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `lathe_blade_corner` (4 tests, each fails before the fix):**\n  - a 3 mm groove at Z-10 posts Z-11.5, Z-8.5 or Z-10 for orientation 2, 1 or 6, and the cache stays at Z-10;\n  - a part-off at Z-20 leaves the part's back face at Z-18.5 for every setting (before the fix, a left-corner blade left 17 mm);\n  - ID and face codes are refused by name;\n  - undo and redo.\n- **Units and round-trip:** a tools unit for the blade chart, and `project_roundtrip::a_blade_corner_round_trips_and_old_blades_take_the_left_corner`.\n- **Regressions, all green:** lathe_nose_tip, lathe_post, lathe_post_g76, lathe_post_refusals, lathe_field_sim, lathe_field_tools, turning, turning_blade, conformance, golden_cl, posting, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, the tool suites, tools lib, and the ui orientation row. Clippy is clean.\n\n**Not exercised:** a Hub run, which comes with the lathe kit after #626.\n\nChangelog: Grooving and parting blades post their touched-off corner (lathe orientation 1 = right, 2 = left (default), 6 = width centre) instead of the blade's width centre; ID/face codes are refused by name (#641)\n\nFixes #641\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
